%% Built (configuration-flow.md); the shaded part is designed (policy-enforcement.md, stages 0, 1, 6), not built.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant KL as Kubelet
    participant PI as polar-init (init container)
    participant AG as Agent process
    participant AB as AgentBuilder
    participant PE as polar-env (Config)
    participant IS as InfrastructureSupervisor
    participant DS as Domain supervisor

    KL->>PI: start, with --cert and --check-dep-cert arguments
    PI->>PI: wait for the dependencies' certificates, get this agent's certificates
    opt the agent needs encryption (POLAR_INIT_ESCROW_BOOTSTRAP)
        PI->>PI: escrow key bootstrap, leave a kernel key handle for the workload
    end
    PI-->>KL: exit 0
    KL->>AG: start, with the environment the resolver derived
    AG->>DS: spawn the domain supervisor
    DS->>AB: new(...).with_...().configure()
    AB->>PE: snapshot of the process environment, declared variables only
    PE-->>AB: values with their sources: env, default, unset
    AB->>AB: judge it: capabilities the code requires against POLAR_CAPABILITIES, each section's variables and relations
    alt any problem
        AB-->>AG: every problem together, process exits non-zero
    else all well
        AB-->>DS: ConfiguredAgent, with the Config
    end
    DS->>DS: read its own settings from the snapshot
    DS->>AB: build()
    AB->>IS: spawn: health, router, subscriptions, Cassini client, crypto
    IS-->>DS: AgentResources, including the same Config

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over AB,IS: DESIGNED (policy-enforcement.md, stages 0, 1 and 6), not built
    AB->>AB: the service name must be the workload name (POLAR_WORKLOAD), else refuse to start
    AB->>AB: the topic set: TOPICS declared, plus implied (the builder's own topics, those NEEDS bring),<br/>the same set --scaffold prints, each implied topic with its rule
    IS->>IS: every subscribe and publish outside the set is refused here, in the agent's log
    IS->>IS: not healthy until a snapshot from the credentials agent is verified<br/>(a bootstrap service is: it runs on the certificate floor until its first)
    end
